    "notes": "D-077 (22 October 2026). User-supplied rerun of the fixed pier model after the user found that the pier wall extra members had followed the soil elevation changes: the four vertical 36 x 60 in wall members now span pile points 2 to 11 (EL 40.20 to the soil surface EL 26.05, 169.8 in) instead of points 2 to 13 (EL 19.72); every other input (nodal and bearing loads, geometry, pile section and material, soil, the four load combinations, the thirty ties) is identical. Wall self-weight in the model 127.3 kip service (31.83 kip per member) in place of 184.4 kip; the CAD wall is 133.4 kip. Cap envelope moves slightly (max M3 365.84 to 361.01 kip-ft, max V2 218.96 to 220.46 kip) and the pile demands follow. The 21 October export is archived under fbmp/pier/archive/2026-10-22/. D-073 (21 October 2026). User-supplied rerun of the fixed pier model: the pipe pile material is ASTM A252 Grade 3, Fy 45 ksi, in place of the 60 ksi of the 19 October export; nodal loads, geometry, pile section, soil and load combinations are unchanged, the cap member forces differ only by solver noise below 1e-7 kip, and the pile failure ratios, the interaction diagram and the output summary follow the 45 ksi material. Exact supplied bytes; the 19 October export is archived under fbmp/pier/archive/2026-10-19/. The pier cap case and the pier pile case are rerun from this export the same day (D-073). See coherence/evidence/2026-10-21-fbmp/source_receipt.json. D-049 supplied bytes retained. D-051 recalculated the cap and exported a matching report/case. Native run records, pile-head review and any other downstream calculations retain their separate status. See coherence/evidence/2026-10-19-cap-rerun/source_receipt.json.",
